---
// Accessibility statement. Lists what was actually done (see the launch hardening pass) and the
// known gaps honestly; a statement that overclaims is worse than none. Update the review date
// whenever the site is re-audited.
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { getSiteSettings } from "../lib/content";

const settings = await getSiteSettings();
const updated = "November 13, 2026";
const sms = `sms:${settings.phoneTel}`;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  heading="Accessibility."
  lede="Everyone should be able to learn about the studio and book a visit. Here is what we have done, and how to reach us if something gets in your way."
  description={`The accessibility statement for the ${settings.businessName} website, and how to get help.`}
  path="/accessibility"
  updated={`Last reviewed ${updated}`}
>
  <h2 id="goal">Our goal</h2>
  <p>
    We aim for this website to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA, the standard most
    widely used to judge whether a website works for people with disabilities.
  </p>

  <h2 id="done">What we have done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every page can be used with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus ring and a "Skip to content" link.</li>
    <li>Pages are built with proper headings, landmarks and labels, so screen readers can move around them.</li>
    <li>Photos have written descriptions, and text and controls meet contrast requirements.</li>
    <li>Animation is gentle, stops if your device asks for reduced motion, and the moving headline can be paused.</li>
    <li>Pages still show all their content if JavaScript does not load.</li>
    <li>
      The appointment form labels every field, explains any mistake in words beside the field, and announces when it has
      sent.
    </li>
    <li>The site is checked with automated accessibility testing (axe) and by hand with a keyboard before changes go live.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="limits">Known limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Photo descriptions in the live Instagram section come from the post captions, which may not describe the photo fully.
    </li>
    <li>
      The Google map is provided by Google and is not fully accessible. The studio address and a directions link are always
      given as text beside it.
    </li>
    <li>Linked websites such as Instagram, Yelp and Google Maps are run by other companies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="help">Get help or tell us about a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If anything on this website is hard to use, or you would like information in another way, please tell us. Pomi can go
    through services, prices, aftercare and booking with you by phone or text, and we will fix the problem on the website.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Call <a href={`tel:${settings.phoneTel}`}>{settings.phone}</a></li>
    <li>Text <a href={sms}>{settings.phone}</a></li>
    <li>Visit {settings.street}, {settings.city}, {settings.state} {settings.zip}</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We aim to reply within two business days.</p>

  <h2 id="studio">At the studio</h2>
  <p>
    If you have access needs for your visit, mention them when you book and we will do our best to make the appointment
    work for you.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
